  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The pin `adaptive_spiral_round_a_part_outside_equals_main_before_3818` failed on macOS aarch64 on main (#3853). It compared a recorded FNV hash of 5687 moves, with each coordinate rounded to 1e-4 mm. The last float bits differ across targets, and the hash changes completely.\n- The Adaptive pin and the Zigzag pin (`zigzag_rows_keep_their_links_round_a_part`, the same class) now compute the same plan with `around_part` off in the same run. That plan never links by the ring law. Each pin asserts the same move count, the same move kinds, the same move ends (exactly) and the same notes. The `digest` helper is removed.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3853-portable-adaptive-pin.md` says why the hash was not portable, and what was dropped.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test pass_start_levels`: 19 passed. The branch includes origin/main with #3855 and #3820.\n- With the predicate `ring_links::rings` removed, both pins are red (\"the move count changed\"). The source was restored after the check.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 1 step (`motion pass_start_levels (pocket_outside::)`), 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- macOS aarch64: not run here. Both sides of each comparison run on the same machine, so the comparison does not depend on the platform.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3853\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
